---
Heat a #10-inch skillet{} over medium heat. Melt @unsalted butter{2.5%Tbsp},
then add three-quarters of the @scallions{5%large} (trimmed and thinly sliced)
and all the @garlic{3.75%cloves} (minced). Cook, stirring frequently, until
softened, about ~{3%minutes}.

Stir in the coarsely chopped @baby spinach leaves{10%oz} in batches if
necessary. Add @kosher salt{5/8%tsp} and cook until the spinach is just wilted,
2 to ~{5%minutes}.

Pour in the @low-sodium vegetable stock{2 1/4%c} and bring to a simmer.
Stir in the @orzo{1 1/4%c}, @lemon zest{1 1/4%tsp}, and the remaining
@kosher salt{5/8%tsp}.

Cover the skillet and reduce heat to medium-low. Simmer until the orzo is nearly
cooked through and most of the liquid has been absorbed, 10 to ~{14%minutes},
stirring once or twice to prevent sticking.

Stir in most of the @feta cheese{15%tbsp} (crumbled), @frozen peas{10%tbsp} (thawed,
optional), and chopped @fresh herbs{1 1/4%c} (dill, parsley, or cilantro). Cover
the pan and cook for ~{1%minute} more to finish the orzo and warm the peas.

Garnish with the reserved scallions and remaining feta. Serve warm.
